  "what": "A real kill mid-ADAPT during the B4 campaign, and its recovery",
  "how": "At ~21:09Z the campaign workers were stopped with SIGTERM to their process groups to deploy a harness fix (marker issues found by listing, not search). Worker w0 was inside ADAPT for CVE-2026-35192 (claude -p running). The stage failed as 'SystemExit: 143' (the killed claude -p never reported its cost: cost_unknown). `heirloom campaign --id b4-replay --continue` re-queued the event; the new run reused every finished stage from the ledger, re-ran ADAPT (attempt 2), then VERIFY, BEHAVIOUR, DECIDE and PUBLISH. A later harness bug (KeyError in the PR claims for reused probes) failed publish.pr after the push; the next --continue reconciled: commit, push and artifacts were cached and the PR was created once (#11).",
